body: "pm-cli now needs its main CHANGELOG.md to be fully generated by pm-changelog across the actual released version history, not only the latest release window and not only tracker release metadata.\\n\\nCurrent behavior in pm-changelog@2026.5.24-11:\\n- latest release range mode works for one section with --release-version-from-package --since-previous-tag --until-release-tag\\n- full output can cover the large tracker (807 items in pm-cli) when no range is passed\\n- --group-by release groups by pm item release metadata, producing headings such as Unreleased/vnext/archive-2026q2 rather than actual git/npm release tags\\n\\nNeeded package-owned behavior:\\n- generate a full Keep a Changelog-style CHANGELOG.md from all relevant git tags, newest first\\n- include an Unreleased section for closed items after the latest tag\\n- derive each released section's date from the tag/commit timestamp\\n- assign pm items to the tag window by item close/update/create timestamp\\n- keep item IDs/link generation and --check support working for large trackers\\n\\nThis should be fixed in pm-changelog, not papered over in pm-cli with a custom script.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-05-24T15:38:50Z)\n>\n> Fixed in pm-changelog@2026.5.24-12. The package now exposes --all-release-tags / --release-tag-pattern through both the standalone CLI and pm extension contract, generates full history from git tag windows with an Unreleased section, and CI fetches tags before changelog checks."
